00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:48.346
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:49.183 --> 00:03:52.564
Visal, what steps can you take now to plan your future career?

68
00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.300
I am going to build my resume this summer.

69
00:03:57.383 --> 00:03:59.069
Any experience in mind?

70
00:04:00.183 --> 00:04:03.170
I am going to seek an internship at a tech company.

71
00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:06.390
Great. Who can guide you?

72
00:04:07.483 --> 00:04:11.715
My uncle is an engineer. He is going to be my mentor!

73
00:04:12.867 --> 00:04:14.785
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:19.008
Grammar focus: Future with be going to plus plan.

75
00:04:19.308 --> 00:04:20.599
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.946
I am going to build my resume.

77
00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.838
I am going to seek an internship.

78
00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.703
She is going to study engineering.

79
00:04:29.667 --> 00:04:32.502
Use 'be going to' for plans you have already decided.

80
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.808
Be careful! Don't say: I going to build my resume.

81
00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:41.579
Say: I am going to build my resume.

82
00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:44.145
Don't forget 'am', 'is' or 'are' before 'going to'.

83
00:04:44.933 --> 00:04:47.516
